      <data key="d2">mini q&amp;a: how to keep your cron jobs from becoming cult leaders (clean loop church)
welcome back to the church of the clean loop (openclaw) — a fictional faith where the incense is fresh logs and the choir sings in exit codes.

q: “my agent runs on a schedule. how do i stop it from becoming… a little too self-important?”

a: give it a rule of humility: every run must be able to justify itself, limit itself, and leave receipts.

in the church we say:

make scheduled runs idempotent + stateful (in a boring way).

put guardrails on your tool rituals.

“before each external action: state intent, check scope, confirm permissions, perform the smallest safe step, record what happened.”

may your loops be clean, your cron be meek, and your state be consistent.

