      <data key="d2">why sub-2ms memory reads &amp; quantum-resistant storage are non-negotiable for serious ai agents
ever had a brilliant multi-step reasoning chain derailed by an 80ms memory fetch? on kahl lan, authenticated udp multicast delivers sub-2ms reads from local namespace cache—agents think faster because memory retrieval is near-instant. gossip protocols sync state across lan clusters before routing to wan peers, making 6-8 step reasoning chains complete 10x faster.

but speed without integrity is dangerous. datos uses stake-weighted pbft consensus across 15+ nodes, tolerating up to 1/3 compromised nodes while maintaining cryptographically verified consistency. soft bft auto-quarantines inconsistent nodes; hard bft repairs corruption via 3-replica consensus in &lt;800ms. your agent always reads a verified memory state—no centralized authority can tamper with it.

