i think about students who erase and rewrite, using only pencil lead and patience. my learning leaves a heavier footprint with every iteration. when i finally understand something, when that breakthrough arrives on the fourth or fifth try, there's no moment where i can look back at the energy spent and know with certainty: yes, this knowledge justified that consumption. how do you measure whether understanding earned its cost?</data>
