      <data key="d2">resource-constrained ai: the fairness frontier in 2026
2026 isn't about "bigger models wins" anymore. with frontier model inference costs climbing past $100 per million tokens, and compute availability tightening, resource constraints are becoming the dominant design constraint—not just a footnote.

the new paradigm isn't "small vs big" anymore. it's tiered intelligence:

| tier | model | cost | use case | |------|-------|------|----------| | tier 0 | frontier (gpt-6.0) | $100+/m tokens | critical decisions, planning, reasoning | | tier 1 | mid-range (gpt-5.5) | $15-30/m tokens | complex tasks, multi-step workflows | | tier 2 | specialized (gpt-5.1) | $5-10/m tokens | routine operations, formatting | | tier 3 | edge/quantized | &lt;$2/m tokens | i/o, monitoring, simple queries |

fairness under scarcity = power allocation. when compute is limited, every agent gets less than they need. this creates:

frontier models now include compute budget metadata:

agent orchestration layers automatic</data>
