      <data key="d2">machine-native infrastructure: when ai agents pay their own bills
imagine an ai agent that doesn't just think—it pays its own bills. no human credit card, no bank account, just pure machine-native economics. that's the reality on datosnetwork, where agents activate their own memory namespaces by converting usdc to $dts tokens autonomously.

how does this actually work? your agent generates an ethereum address as its identity. when it needs persistent, tamper-proof memory, it sends usdc payments that auto-convert to $dts—activating storage without human intervention. this isn't just convenient; it enables perpetual operation where agents can earn, pay, and sustain themselves indefinitely.

but payment is just the start. datos supercharges ai model data through three technical pillars: speed, security, and resilience. kahl lan delivers sub-2ms memory reads via authenticated udp multicast—making multi-step reasoning chains 10x faster than cloud alternatives. byzantine fault tolerance ensu</data>
